// Title: Volume Image Creation Via Disk2vhd
// Sigma ID: 7b5668f7-e7d9-4845-a935-18aa6ce9ff40
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: EinLamYe
// Date: 2026-06-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, collection, T1003.003, T1005
// Description: Detects execution of the Sysinternals Disk2vhd tool, which clones a live volume into a VHD/VHDX.
//   Adversaries abuse it to obtain an offline copy of a system volume (e.g. a Domain Controller's C:
//   containing NTDS.dit and the SAM/SYSTEM hives) for offline credential extraction.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate virtual machine migration or backup by administrators
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/disk2vhd
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/8e7b36a9de00c979a098f16eb29c1c22fb63cb4b/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_disk2vhd_volume_image.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\disk2vhd.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "Disk2Vhd.exe"
